"I must admit, corn is my favorite vegetable, especially when it is still on the cob. Cooking corn is very simple. First, it is removed from the husk and any hair is pulled off. Then it is placed into a pot of boiling water and left to simmer until the kernels are tender. It can also be barbequed with the husk still on. The husk holds juices inside and keeps the corn from drying out on the barbeque.": "dc4764e961b8",
